 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:10:32.519308Z",
 "text": "Yes, this clause is enforceable. Under section 108 of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, neither a landlord nor a tenancy agreement may **require** a tenant to provide post-dated cheques or permit automatic debiting (pre-authorized debit) for the payment of rent. However, the Act does not prohibit a tenant from voluntarily choosing to use these payment methods. Because the clause explicitly makes both options voluntary and states that the tenant is not required to use either method, it complies with section 108.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 108",
